    "summary": "Large, wooden dance mask, &quot;nimba&quot;, in the form of a woman&#039;s head and torso. The head is elongated, the features being emphasised with lines of white metal upholstery studs. Raffia tassels are attached to the ears and chin. The elaborate coiffure, with raised median crest, is defined by incised chevron marks. The torso features carved elongated breasts and ends in four wooden struts which fit over the masquerader&#039;s shoulders.",
